    "body": "This is not talking about pairs though. This is talking about after you convert a JavaScript string to code points at which point the only surrogates left are in fact isolated. That might be a little confusing, but I don't think the proposed fix helps alleviate that confusion (e.g., the definition of noncharacters is also in terms of code points and doesn't make sense if we assume the definition of surrogates is about code units).",
